⁧סוכות⁩⁦,⁩ ⁧זמן שמחתנו⁩. The ⁧יום טוב⁩ which we celebrate by completely removing
ourselves from our homes and comfort and placing our complete trust in
the hands of Hashem, going out into a little ⁦סוכה'לה⁩. What is this ⁧שמחה⁩
representing, what is it related to? This ⁧שמחה⁩ is related to ⁧הכרת הטוב⁩.
We're thanking Hashem for the ⁧ענני הכבוד⁩ and for the ⁧סוכות⁩ they had in
⁧מצרים⁩. We're thanking Hashem for ⁧יציאת מצרים⁩⁦,⁩ of course. Through all the
⁧דורות⁩⁦,⁩ we're thanking Hashem for all of the ⁧ניסים ונפלאות⁩ which he has
done for us, represented by our otherworldly existence in the
⁧סוכה⁩\. What's going to happen when ⁧משיח⁩ comes? When ⁧משיח⁩ comes, the ⁧גוים⁩
are going to be jealous of us. Everybody knows the ⁧מדרש⁩. The ⁧גמרא⁩ in
⁧עבודה זרה⁩ mentions that Hashem will tell all the nations of the world, “I'm bringing ⁧משיח⁩” and the ⁧גוים⁩ will say, “Hey, if we would have had a
⁧מצוה⁩⁦,⁩ we would have done it.” Hashem will say, “Okay, I'll give you an
easy ⁧מצוה⁩⁦,⁩” and He'll give them the ⁧מצוה⁩ of ⁧סוכה⁩⁦,⁩ which they will
proceed to demolish. They're not interested in the ⁧מצוה⁩ of ⁧סוכה⁩. The
question is, what does ⁧סוכה⁩ have to do with the ⁧גוים⁩? Why specifically
this “easy ⁧מצוה⁩”?

R’ Kormornick, #metadata(none) <person-index-r-kormornick-1009> in his second sefer of A Short Vort, #metadata(none) <person-index-a-short-vort-1008> brings a beautiful
connection between ⁧סוכה⁩ and ⁧הכרת הטוב⁩ and the ⁧גוים⁩. What is the ⁧יום טוב⁩
of ⁧סוכות⁩? What are all the ⁧קרבנות⁩? There are 70 ⁧קרבנות⁩. We, little
Yidden, are bringing ⁧ברכה⁩ to the world through our ⁧בית המקדש⁩ and ⁧קרבנות⁩.
We're giving the ⁧גוים⁩ a ⁧ברכה⁩. This ⁧סוכה⁩ represents the ⁧ברכה⁩ that we're
giving the ⁧גוים⁩. They should show a little gratitude and a little
respect, but they don't. They don't know what it means to have
gratitude. That is a Yiddish trait; it's not a ⁧גויישע⁩ trait. When we
have ⁧הכרת הטוב⁩⁦,⁩ it deepens our love for ⁧הקדוש ברוך הוא⁩. If you want to
love somebody, you give them. We give Hashem our ⁧עבודה⁩. Why? Because
Hashem gives us everything. ⁧סוכות⁩ will be a test of the ⁧גוים⁩ and they
will fail miserably, and since we celebrate ⁧סוכות⁩⁦,⁩ we are passing
magnificently.

This ⁧מדה⁩ of ⁧הכרת הטוב⁩ is exemplified in a story with R’ Moshe Schwab.#metadata(none) <person-index-r-moshe-schwab-1010> R’
Moshe Schwab#metadata(none) <person-index-r-moshe-schwab-1011> once decided to walk to a ⁧שלום זכר⁩ of a distant
acquaintance that he really did not know. It was a long walk, he was an
old man. When asked by his family why he was making this difficult walk
to someone he really did not know that well, he answered that he did not
remember but he was told that his own ⁧שלום זכר⁩ which welcomed him into
the world when he was born fell on the first night of ⁧פסח⁩. On the first
night of ⁧פסח⁩⁦,⁩ everyone was busy with their seder - only one person came
to R’ Moshe Schwab's#metadata(none) <person-index-r-moshe-schwab-1012> ⁧שלום זכר⁩. That person was this new baby's
great-grandfather. Because ⁧הכרת הטוב⁩ is such an important ⁧מדה⁩⁦,⁩ he did
not want to miss the opportunity to demonstrate his appreciation to that
family for that beautiful thing.

That is ⁧גדלות⁩. That is sensitivity. That is something we can learn from
and hope to emulate.

